(Tessel Foundation Annual Report 2024) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
16 TL
(This report summarises the Tessel Foundation's work, finances and projects for) Tj T*
(the calendar year 2024. It was approved by the steering committee, chaired in) Tj T*
(2024 by Ana Lindqvist, at its February 2025 meeting.) Tj T*
T*
(Highlights. The foundation's two projects both shipped major releases in 2024.) Tj T*
(Quillstate 2.0 was released in February, and LumenDB 3.0 in March, followed by) Tj T*
(LumenDB 3.2 in September. The security team handled one advisory for LumenDB) Tj T*
(during the year and published it with a coordinated fix.) Tj T*
T*
(Sponsors and income. In 2024 the foundation was supported by 27 sponsoring) Tj T*
(organisations, up from 19 in 2023. Total income for 2024 was EUR 412,000.) Tj T*
(Sponsorships provided EUR 301,000, individual donations EUR 87,000, and income) Tj T*
(from the Embedded Data Days workshop EUR 24,000.) Tj T*
T*
(Spending. Total spending for 2024 was EUR 365,000, leaving a surplus of EUR) Tj T*
(47,000 that is held as a reserve for future security work. The largest single) Tj T*
(expense was external security audits of LumenDB and Quillstate, which cost EUR) Tj T*
(96,000. Maintainer stipends cost EUR 84,000, continuous integration and hosting) Tj T*
(infrastructure EUR 58,000, and travel support for contributors EUR 31,000. The) Tj T*
(remaining EUR 96,000 covered legal, accounting and administrative costs.) Tj T*
T*
(Governance. The steering committee met eleven times in 2024. It approved four) Tj T*
(RFCs, including the LumenDB snapshot-pinning RFC adopted for version 3.2. All) Tj T*
(decisions were recorded on the public mailing list. The next steering committee) Tj T*
(election is scheduled for March 2025, when two of the five seats are up for) Tj T*
(election.) Tj T*
T*
(Security. The private security team received six vulnerability reports in 2024.) Tj T*
(Five were found not to be vulnerabilities or were already fixed. One led to a) Tj T*
(published advisory for LumenDB's backup restore function. The foundation plans) Tj T*
(to repeat external audits every two years.) Tj T*
T*
(New projects. In November 2024 the steering committee accepted Driftwood, a) Tj T*
(structured logging library for Rust applications, as the foundation's third) Tj T*
(project. Driftwood was created in 2023 by Lena Hartmann and will move its) Tj T*
(repository to the foundation in early 2025. No other project applications were) Tj T*
(received in 2024.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
